// Reads right's `once` through a bare selective import, and right reads this
// file's the same way. So BOTH edges of the pair are bare `once` mentions and
// neither has any other spelling to fall back on — which is what makes this the
// witness that the edge is load-bearing rather than belt-and-braces. Drop the
// *ast.OnceBinding registration from fileIndex.byDecl and the reference graph
// sees no cycle at all.
//
// The reads are inside functions rather than in the `once` RHSs, so the program
// has no VALUE cycle: only the two files' reference graph is cyclic, and Nomi
// permits that deliberately.
import right.seed

pub once ours: Int = 3

pub fn from_left(): Int {
    seed + ours
}
